{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Who pardons</b> — The sense: for on account of his iniquity he was a son of death, and HaShem rebuked him with diseases to chastise him, to turn him back to be comforted over his iniquity, and to redeem him from the pit. This is explicit in the words of Elihu. The yod of עוניכי (your iniquities) corresponds to the yod of תחלואיכי (your diseases) — an additional elegant turn of phrase."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 103, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:37:57.122118564Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}